      "section": "opening",
      "slot": "opening",
      "text": "Aspose.Slides FOSS for .NET reads and writes presentations in the PPTX format. It creates new presentations, opens existing ones from a path or a stream, and saves presentations to a path or a stream. It supports adding and manipulating slides, sections, shapes including autoShapes, tables, and text with full formatting, as well as fill, line, effect, 3-D, notes, comments, and document properties."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:001",
        "example:009",
        "public_symbol:aspose.slides.foss"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:1",
      "text": "It creates new presentations from scratch, adds slides, inserts shapes with text, and saves the result as a .pptx file, or opens an existing presentation to read and modify its content."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:001",
        "example:006",
        "public_symbol:aspose.slides.foss"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:2",
      "text": "It adds auto shapes such as rectangles, sets their fill color and effects like outer shadow, blur radius, and distance, then saves the formatted shapes to a presentation file."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:003",
        "public_symbol:aspose.slides.foss"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:3",
      "text": "It formats text by setting font height, bold style, Latin font, and fill color on portions, and aligns paragraphs within text frames attached to shapes."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:004",
        "public_symbol:aspose.slides.foss"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:4",
      "text": "It creates tables with specified column widths and row heights, populates cells with text, and merges cells horizontally to build structured layouts."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:008",
        "public_symbol:aspose.slides.foss"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:5",
      "text": "It adds empty slides based on layout slides and organizes slides into named sections such as Introduction and Detail."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:007",
        "public_symbol:aspose.slides.foss"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:6",
      "text": "It adds notes slides with text content and attaches comments to slides with a specified author, position, and timestamp."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:009",
        "public_symbol:aspose.slides.foss"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:7",
      "text": "It saves presentations to a memory stream and reloads them from the same stream without writing to disk."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:aspose.slides.foss"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:8",
      "text": "It preserves unknown or unmodified parts of a presentation when reading and writing files, ensuring round-trip fidelity."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "example:001"
      ],
      "section": "quick_start",
      "slot": "lead_in",
      "text": "This example creates a new presentation, adds a rectangle shape with text to the first slide, saves it as a PPTX file, reopens the file, and prints the slide count, shape count, and text content to the console."
    },
